<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <!--
      ARCHITECTURE.md §8: the per-app proxy picker has to enumerate installed
      apps, and from API 30 a package list is invisible without this. Declared
      here rather than in :app for the same reason :service declares its own
      permissions: the permission belongs next to the one class that needs it,
      which is InstalledAppsSource.

      A <queries> element filtering on a LAUNCHER intent would avoid the
      permission, and was rejected: it omits apps with no launcher activity that
      still use the network, and a user cannot exclude an app the picker does not
      show. A silently partial list reads as a bug, not as a policy.

      §14.7's distribution targets are GitHub Releases and IzzyOnDroid, neither of
      which cares. Nothing here forecloses Play — VPN clients are an accepted use
      case for this permission, and that is a Console declaration rather than a
      code change.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES" />

</manifest>
